# Trading Intelligence Engine Architecture

## Vision

The Trading Intelligence Engine is a modular market analysis framework that transforms raw market data into structured trading intelligence.

The project is designed around independent engines, where each engine has a single responsibility and produces immutable outputs for the next stage of the pipeline.

---

## High-Level Architecture

```
Market Data
    │
    ▼
Data Layer
│
├── Providers
├── Validation
└── Normalization
    │
    ▼
Analysis Layer
│
├── Swing Engine
├── Market Structure
├── Structure Analysis
├── BOS
├── CHOCH
├── Trend
├── Structural Levels
├── Structural Strength
├── Liquidity (Upcoming)
├── Supply & Demand (Upcoming)
├── Order Blocks (Upcoming)
├── Fair Value Gaps (Upcoming)
└── Decision Engine (Future)
```

---

## Design Principles

- Modular architecture
- Immutable domain models
- Pure business logic
- Configuration-driven behavior
- Test-first development
- Evidence-based scoring
- Independent intelligence engines

---

## Core Layers

### Data Layer

Responsible for obtaining and preparing market data.

Responsibilities:

- Download data
- Normalize formats
- Validate datasets

---

### Intelligence Layer

Converts price action into structured market intelligence.

Every engine:

- receives immutable input
- performs one responsibility
- returns immutable output

---

### Decision Layer

Future layer responsible for combining all intelligence into actionable trading decisions.